<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Semicon 1996 net up 28.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Semicon 1996 net up 28.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-December 1996</p>
<p>			    (in million T$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Turnover				39,400   vs    28,766</p>
<p>    Net profit			    19,401   vs    15,081</p>
<p>Note - Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Corp is Taiwan's largest semiconductor maker. A company statement on Tuesday said its earnings per share were T$7.31 in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;TSMC had a great year in 1996, especially in contrast to the industry as a whole,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The firm's 1996 sales revenues grew 37 percent to hit a record T$39.4 billion, compared to a 10 percent decline in sales for the semiconductor industry, the statement said.</p>
<p>The figures were unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
